Phase 0 — Shared building blocks (`@backend-dev`)

- [ ] Add `com.jeet.rest.ApiResponseFactory` (`@ApplicationScoped`) with:
  - [ ] `ok(Object body)` success builder, defaulting to `200` (sets
        `MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON`).
  - [ ] `ok(Object body, Response.Status status)` success builder overload for non-`200` success
        responses (e.g. `201`).
  - [ ] Error builder accepting a `Response.Status`/status code plus an error body.
- [ ] Add a standalone unit test for `ApiResponseFactory` (status code + body + content type for
      both success overloads and the error builder), independent of any controller.

Phase 1 — Movie list family (`@backend-dev`)

- [ ] Create `MovieController`, `MovieService`, `MovieMapper` (`@ApplicationScoped`).
- [ ] Add top-level records: `MovieSummaryItem`, `MovieListResponse`, `TrendingMovieItem`,
      `TrendingMoviesResponse` (reuse from the trending-movies-response-records feature if already
      implemented — do not duplicate).
- [ ] Add `TrendingMoviesParams` `@BeanParam` class (`days`, `limit` query params with defaults).
- [ ] Add a paging-params `@BeanParam` class for `getAllMoviesWithPaging`.
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/movies` (`getAllMovies`) — root key `movies`.
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/movies/paging` (`getAllMoviesWithPaging`) — root key `movies`,
      via the new paging `@BeanParam`.
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/movies/{name}/{order}` (`searchMovies`) — root key
      `searchedMovies`.
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/movies/search` (`fullTextSearchMovies`) — root key
      `searchedMovies`.
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/venue/movies` (`getMoviesForVenue`) — root key `movies`; single
      `locationId` query param stays on plain `@QueryParam` (no `@BeanParam` needed).
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/trending-movies` (`getTrendingMovies`) — root key
      `trendingMovies`, via `TrendingMoviesParams`.
- [ ] Wire all six `MovieController` methods to build success/validation-error `Response`s via
      `ApiResponseFactory`.
- [ ] Remove the six migrated routes and their inline JSON assembly from `BookController`.
- [ ] Verify root keys (`movies`, `searchedMovies`, `trendingMovies`) and item field
      names/types are byte-for-byte unchanged (capture before/after curl output per endpoint).

Phase 2 — Venue/location + screen admin family (`@backend-dev`)

- [ ] Create `VenueController`, `VenueService`.
- [ ] Add `VenueScreeningItem` record + one mapper method reused by three admin
      movies-on-venues endpoints (see below).
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/venue/{movieId}` (`getVenuesForMovie`).
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/venue/v2/{movieId}` (`getLocationForMovie`).
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/locations/venue` (`getLocationForVenue`).
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/locations` (`getAllLocation`).
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/admin/moviesonvenues` (`getAllMoviesOnAllVenues`) — using
      `VenueScreeningItem` mapper.
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/admin/moviesonvenuescategorized`
      (`getAllMoviesOnAllVenuesWithCategory`) — same mapper as above.
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/admin/moviesonvenuessearch` (`getAllMoviesOnAllVenuesForSearch`)
      — same mapper as above.
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/dates/{locationId}/{movieId}` (`getDatesForMovieOnVenue`) — add a
      `@BeanParam` class for its two path params.
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/seats/{screeningDateId}` (`getSeatsForScreenForMovieOnVenue`).
- [ ] Migrate `POST /rest/book/admin/addscreen` (`addScreen`) — introduce a response record for
      the success/`409 CONFLICT` bodies; leave the async Kafka publish call and its error handling
      unchanged.
- [ ] Migrate `POST /rest/book/admin/updatescreen` (`updateScreen`) — same treatment as
      `addScreen`.
- [ ] Migrate `DELETE /rest/book/admin/deletescreen` (`deleteScreen`) — same treatment as
      `addScreen`.
- [ ] For each endpoint above, introduce a record only where manual JSON assembly exists today;
      leave entity-returning endpoints unchanged.
- [ ] Wire all twelve `VenueController` methods to use `ApiResponseFactory`.
- [ ] Remove the twelve migrated routes and inline JSON assembly from `BookController`.
- [ ] Verify JSON shape unchanged per endpoint (before/after curl comparison).

Phase 3 — Purchases/tickets family (`@backend-dev`)

- [ ] Create `PurchaseController`; confirm naming/package for the service layer (existing
      `com.jeet.booking.PurchaseService` already has `getBrainTreeCustomer` — decide whether to
      extend it in place or introduce a differently-scoped service, to avoid ambiguity with
      `CheckoutService`'s own use of `PurchaseService` in Phase 4).
- [ ] Add `PurchaseSummaryItem`, `TicketSummaryItem` records + mapper(s).
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/purchases` (`getAllPurchases`) — root key `purchases`.
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/purchases/tickets` (`getTicketsPerPurchase`).
- [ ] Migrate `POST /rest/book/managepurchases` (`cancelTicket`) — add a `@BeanParam` class for
      its combined header/body-derived inputs if more than one bound input remains after moving
      parsing into the service.
- [ ] Migrate `POST /rest/book/deletepurchases` (`deletePurchase`).
- [ ] Wire all four `PurchaseController` methods to use `ApiResponseFactory`.
- [ ] Remove the four migrated routes and inline JSON assembly from `BookController`.
- [ ] Verify JSON shape unchanged per endpoint.

Phase 4 — Checkout family (`@backend-dev`, payment-path review)

- [ ] Create `CheckoutController`, `CheckoutService`.
- [ ] Add `CheckoutService.reserveSeats(...)` — seat-array parsing loop,
      `ticketService.reserveTickets(...)`, running amount/tax totals, rollback-on-failure via
      `ticketService.rollbackTickets(...)`.
- [ ] Add `CheckoutService.chargeAndFinalize(...)` — Braintree customer id resolution,
      `TransactionRequest` construction, `paymentService.processTransaction(...)`,
      rollback-on-failure.
- [ ] Add `FullCheckoutParams` `@BeanParam` class (header `uuid`; form `orderId`,
      `seatsToBeReserved`, `payment_method_nonce`) with a validation helper method; no business
      logic on the class itself.
- [ ] Add response record(s) for `fullcheckout2`'s success path (`ResponseText`, `purchaseId`,
      `AuthCode`, `ResponseCode`, `Status`, `Amount`, `TaxAmount`, `Success`, `tickets`,
      `seatsforscreen`).
- [ ] Migrate `POST /rest/book/payment/fullcheckout2` (`fullcheckout2`) — bind via
      `FullCheckoutParams` → validate → call `CheckoutService` → map result to response record →
      return via `ApiResponseFactory`; keep existing error-path JSON (missing-params, transaction
      failure) unchanged in shape.
- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/payment/clientToken` (`clientToken`) into `CheckoutController`.
- [ ] Remove the two migrated routes and inline JSON assembly from `BookController`.
      (`webcheckout` and `getMovieTicket` no longer exist in `BookController` and are not part of
      this phase.)
- [ ] Verify JSON shape and status codes unchanged (success and error branches) for both
      endpoints.

Phase 5 — Service extraction from BookingHandlerImpl (`@backend-dev`)

- [ ] Move remaining DTO/domain-shaping methods out of `BookingHandlerImpl` into
      `MovieService`/`VenueService`/`PurchaseService`/`CheckoutService`, matching the endpoints
      migrated in Phases 1-4.
- [ ] Update `TicketService`'s `BookingHandlerImpl` injection to use the new service(s) it
      actually needs.
- [ ] Update `HibernateTest.java`'s direct `new BookingHandlerImpl()` usage (or remove/replace it
      if it becomes dead code).
- [ ] Confirm no remaining references to `BookingHandlerImpl` outside itself.
- [ ] Delete `BookingHandlerImpl.java`.

Phase 6 — Trivial/leftover (`@backend-dev`)

- [ ] Migrate `GET /rest/book/hello` (`getGreeting`) opportunistically — not a dedicated phase,
      only if low effort (e.g. alongside `MovieController`).
- [ ] Confirm `BookController` is empty/removed once all 25 endpoints are migrated, or document
      which endpoints remain and why.

Phase 7 — Bulk verification (all at once, no intermediate compile per REQ-ALL-6/NF-2)

- [ ] Complete Phases 0-6 in one pass without stopping to compile in between.
- [ ] `cd mbooks-quarkus && mvn -DskipTests compile` once, after all phases are done.
- [ ] `cd mbooks-quarkus && mvn -DskipTests package` for a full module build.
- [ ] Run any existing endpoint tests covering migrated methods.
- [ ] Re-run before/after curl comparisons for every one of the 25 migrated endpoints in one
      consolidated pass.
- [ ] Confirm `mbooks-quarkus/README.md` endpoint documentation still matches actual behavior (no
      rewrite expected; update only on discovered drift).
- [ ] If bulk verification surfaces regressions, revert from the pre-migration git commit.
